---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Rule from "../components/Rule.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import rows from "../data/gaps.json";
---
<Base title="What we cannot close"
      eyebrow={`${rows.length} of them`}
      dek="Not the same page as the open questions. These are the places where the work has been done properly and the record may simply not exist — where more effort is not obviously the answer.">

<section class="blk">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>An archive that lists only its questions implies they are all answerable. Some are not. A parish
      register with a gap in it, a marriage in a country nobody has narrowed, a farm held on a lease that
      left no title &mdash; these do not yield to persistence.</p>
    <p><strong>Each row says what was actually done</strong>, so that nobody repeats it, and then says
      plainly what would have to exist for the gap to be closable at all.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<Rule name="arrows" label="Unfinished, and possibly unfinishable" />

<section class="blk">
  {rows.map(r => (
    <div class="panel" style="margin-top:20px">
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:1.08rem"><strong>{r.gap}</strong></p>
      <p style="margin:12px 0 0"><span class="lab">What has been done</span><br />{r.what_has_been_done}</p>
      <p style="margin:12px 0 0"><span class="lab">Why it may never close</span><br />{r.why_it_may_never_close}</p>
    </div>
  ))}
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="note">These are distinct from the <a href={u("/open-questions/")}>open questions</a>, which
    are answerable and merely unanswered, and from the <a href={u("/hypotheses/")}>hypotheses</a>, which
    are propositions this archive is entertaining without having proved.</div>
</section>
</Base>
